-- title:
--   Trivial symbol forces the norm into the norm-ray subgroup
-- statement:
--   Let $L/K$ be an extension of number fields with $L/K$ Galois and $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ commutative, let $\mathfrak f$ be an ideal of $\mathcal O_K$, and let $i$ be an element of the set `primeCarriers K 𝔣`, i.e. an element of the group $I_K^{\mathfrak f}$ of invertible fractional ideals of $K$ whose valuation vanishes at every prime dividing $\mathfrak f$ which is of the form `primeUnit K v` for a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_K$ with $v \nmid \mathfrak f$. Let $c$ be an `ArtinFieldCore K L 𝔣 i`: a datum consisting of number fields $E, N, \Theta$ with $K \subseteq E \subseteq N$, $L \subseteq N$, $N \subseteq \Theta$, with $N/E$ and $\Theta/E$ Galois with commutative Galois groups, a modulus $\mathfrak m$ of $\mathcal O_K$ divisible by $\mathfrak f$, a prime $v \nmid \mathfrak m$ whose carrier in $I_K^{\mathfrak f}$ is $i$, a prime $w$ of $\mathcal O_E$ above $v$ with $w \nmid \mathfrak m \mathcal O_E$ and residue degree $1$, an integer $q \neq 0$ with $q \mathcal O_E \mid \mathfrak m\mathcal O_E$ and a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta \in \Theta$ generating $\Theta$ over $E$, together with the further components `Ip`, `ωpi` and `Ni` of the structure. Assume: (i) `SecondInequalityCTM` for $N/E$ at the extended modulus $\mathfrak m\mathcal O_E$, that is, the index of the norm-ray subgroup of $I_E^{\mathfrak m\mathcal O_E}$ attached to $N/E$ divides $\#\mathrm{Gal}(N/E)$; and (ii) for every intermediate field $F$ of $N/E$ with $[F:E]$ prime, `FirstInequalityCTM`, that is, $\#\mathrm{Gal}(F/E)$ divides the index of the norm-ray subgroup of $I_E^{\mathfrak m\mathcal O_E}$ attached to $F/E$. Then for every $x$ in `c.Ip` with `c.ωpi x = 1`, the element `c.Ni x` lies in `normRaySubgroup K L 𝔣`, the subgroup of $I_K^{\mathfrak f}$ generated by the narrow ray subgroup of $K$ at $\mathfrak f$ (intersected with $I_K^{\mathfrak f}$) together with the image of the relative norm `relNormCTM K L 𝔣` from $I_L^{\mathfrak f \mathcal O_L}$.
--
--   This is the kernel half of Artin's proof of the reciprocity law by crossing with auxiliary cyclotomic fields: an element of the auxiliary datum on which the symbol is trivial has norm lying in the norm-ray subgroup downstairs, the two class-field-theoretic inequalities upstairs and on the prime-degree layers being what makes the descent work. It feeds the statements that the Artin symbol is surjective with kernel exactly the norm-ray subgroup, for moduli dividing $24$ and for admissible moduli of given degree, and the construction of transfer data in degree three.
